      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Humboldt_Hill%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Humboldt County Historical Society, founded in the 1940s, preserves the region’s heritage in a former home of Helen Wells Barnum.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.humboldthistory.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Since its founding, the society’s membership has grown to over two thousand dedicated volunteers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.humboldthistory.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Its archives boast more than 65,000 photographs, hundreds of historic maps, and unique business and criminal ledgers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.humboldthistory.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The society publishes a quarterly magazine, the Humboldt Historian, and maintains a reference library for researchers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.humboldthistory.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Visitors can explore the society’s digital collection of 1930s‑1950s moving images, showcasing everyday life in Humboldt County.",
